Z||000005||p4n1c||03-01-2001||02:46 PM||||hahaha, my girlfriend calls hers a jeep too.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  They are so far from a jeep, jeeps don't roll on low-speed sharp turns.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>4.3?!?!  Holy sh$$  It would be like a gocart that could break the sound barrier.<P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>"Each passing day, every passing face seems like such a blur" <BR>- The Offspring(Million Miles Away)<p>[This message has been edited by p4n1c (edited 03-01-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000006||jlhuber||03-01-2001||05:47 PM||||Calling a Tracker a JEEP?!?!?  That is like calling an Explorer a Suburban.  They may look like the same "type" of vehicle to the untrained eye, but to those of us who know better they are not.<P>I was reading in an off-road magazine where GM (I believe it was GM) made a prototype/custom Tracker by stuffing in a 4.3, put a suspension lift with 33 BFGs under it, 5-point harnesses, and a couple of other things too.  Now that would be a cool toy to have.  As far as I know, the Tracker was never offered with a 4.3.<P>Oh yeah, speaking of fast go-karts.  Kawasaki developed a 125cc single that would propell a racing kart to 110mph.  While sitting 1/2 inch off the ground, now that had to seem fast.  I am not into racing karts so I don't know if that is fast for them, but it seems fast to me.<BR>------------------<BR>--Jess--<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/blackeye2/double0smile.gif">     <BR>If you expect the unexpected, was it really even unexpected in the first place?<p>[This message has been edited by jlhuber (edited 03-01-2001).]||||reg||1
